@startuml
title Composite / Part-Whole

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Compose objects into trees; treat leaves and composites uniformly.

**Motivation**:
Tree-like structures (file systems, UI components, organizational hierarchies).

**Applicability**:
Recursive composition required; clients treat groups and items uniformly.

**Participants**:
Component common interface; Leaf and Composite implement it.

**Consequences**:
Pros: Uniform treatment; easy to add new component types.
Cons: Can make constraints harder (e.g., limiting child types).

**Implementation Notes**:
Manage parent references, iteration, and validation.
Combine with Iterator for traversal and Visitor for operations.

**Known Uses**:
Swing/JavaFX scene graphs; DOM trees.

**Related Patterns**: Iterator, Visitor, Decorator.

endlegend

interface Component {
  +operation()
}

class Leaf
class Composite {
  +operation()
  +add(c: Component)
  +remove(c: Component)
  -children : List<Component>
}

Component <|.. Leaf
Component <|.. Composite
Composite *-- Component : children
@enduml